h}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/deployments","created_at":"2020-06-24T21:50:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T13:39:00Z","pushed_at":"2024-06-05T09:00:53Z","git_url":"git://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:cisagov/crossfeed.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed","homepage":"https://docs.crossfeed.cyber.dhs.gov","size":84021,"stargazers_count":417,"watchers_count":417,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":65,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":342,"license":{"key":"cc0-1.0","name":"Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal","spdx_id":"CC0-1.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/cc0-1.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTY="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cybersecurity","infrastructure","scanning"],"visibility":"public","forks":65,"open_issues":342,"watchers":417,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/pulls/1490","html_url":"https://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed/pull/1490","diff_url":"https://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed/pull/1490.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cisagov/crossfeed/pull/1490.patch","merged_at":"2022-08-21T14:22:44Z"},"body":"Bumps [mitmproxy](https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy) from 8.0.0 to 8.1.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/releases\">mitmproxy's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.1.1</h2>\n<p>Changes: See <a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>.\nYou can find the latest release packages at <a href=\"https://mitmproxy.org/downloads/\">https://mitmproxy.org/downloads/</a>.</p>\n<h2>v8.1.0</h2>\n<p>Changes: See <a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>.\nYou can find the latest release packages at <a href=\"https://mitmproxy.org/downloads/\">https://mitmproxy.org/downloads/</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">mitmproxy's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>28 June 2022: mitmproxy 8.1.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Support specifying the local address for outgoing connections\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/discussions/5364\">#5364</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/meitinger\"><code>@​meitinger</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix a bug where an excess empty chunk has been sent for chunked HEAD request.\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/discussions/5372\">#5372</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/jixunmoe\"><code>@​jixunmoe</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Drop pkg_resources dependency.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5401\">#5401</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/PavelICS\"><code>@​PavelICS</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix huge (&gt;65kb) http2 responses corrupted.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5428\">#5428</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/dhabensky\"><code>@​dhabensky</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Remove overambitious assertions in the HTTP state machine,\nfix some error handling.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5383\">#5383</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Use default_factory for parser_options.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5474\">#5474</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/rathann\"><code>@​rathann</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>15 May 2022: mitmproxy 8.1.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>DNS support\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pull/5232\">#5232</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/meitinger\"><code>@​meitinger</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Mitmproxy now requires Python 3.9 or above.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5233\">#5233</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix a memory leak in mitmdump where flows were kept in memory.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4786\">#4786</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Replayed flows retain their current position in the flow list.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5227\">#5227</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Periodically send HTTP/2 ping frames to keep connections alive.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5046\">#5046</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/EndUser509\"><code>@​EndUser509</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Console Performance Improvements\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/3427\">#3427</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/BkPHcgQL3V\"><code>@​BkPHcgQL3V</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Warn users if server side event responses are received without streaming.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4469\">#4469</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add flatpak support to the browser addon\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5200\">#5200</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/pauloromeira\"><code>@​pauloromeira</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add example addon to dump contents to files based on a filter expression\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5190\">#5190</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/redraw\"><code>@​redraw</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix a bug where the wrong SNI is sent to an upstream HTTPS proxy\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5109\">#5109</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Make sure that mitmproxy displays error messages on startup.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5225\">#5225</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add example addon for domain fronting.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5217\">#5217</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/randomstuff\"><code>@​randomstuff</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Improve cut addon to better handle binary contents\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/3965\">#3965</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/mhils\"><code>@​mhils</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix text truncation for full-width characters\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4278\">#4278</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/kjy00302\"><code>@​kjy00302</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Fix mitmweb export copy failed in non-secure domain.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5264\">#5264</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/Pactortester\"><code>@​Pactortester</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add example script for manipulating cookies.\n(<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5278\">#5278</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/WillahScott\"><code>@​WillahScott</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/564d439df8ffd53198f1776b603223f5185bdcba\"><code>564d439</code></a> bump to 8.1.1</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/c779230ba15542320871816ae6b88ce17ba17c80\"><code>c779230</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5438\">#5438</a> from mitmproxy/pyinstaller</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/d003038803a8afd45bf33d9917773d7ea24deded\"><code>d003038</code></a> fix nits</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/3a2b02b420c6fba2b90568fc3e4081cf1ccb2739\"><code>3a2b02b</code></a> don't error on connection errors when streaming, fix <a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5383\">#5383</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/8ffd2dcaaa8c02eb009e1198049940e9d2a20a42\"><code>8ffd2dc</code></a> windows installer: use 64bit builds</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/6704407026326a06a4c20aee118f9add3e4e422d\"><code>6704407</code></a> bump dependencies</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/87d3d1cb88efc63476787f7facd6eb4c9dcadf8b\"><code>87d3d1c</code></a> pyinstaller: move hooks into package</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/661b7565207148bbeb926bc58932ed8ff978529e\"><code>661b756</code></a> don't display an error if urwid cannot determine the encoding, fix <a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5413\">#5413</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/82f18f6afb40e23d2d4aff526de6a9d718811de1\"><code>82f18f6</code></a> fix huge (&gt;65kb) http2 responses corrupted (<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5430\">#5430</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/commit/0737c68289c2dc7974ee0696367393b6544af386\"><code>0737c68</code></a> accept newer protobuf versions (<a href=\"https://github-redirect.dependabot.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/5429\">#5429</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/compare/v8.0.0...v8.1.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=mitmproxy&package-manager=pip&previous-version=8.0.0&new-version=8.1.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\nDependabot will merge this PR once CI passes on it, as requested by @epicfaace.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot merge` will merge this PR after your CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot squash and merge` will squash and merge this PR after your CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot cancel merge` will cancel a previously requested merge and block automerging\n- `@dependabot reopen` will reopen this PR if it is closed\n- `@dependabot close` will close this PR and stop Dependabot recreating it. You can achieve the same result by closing it manually\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/issues/1490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cisagov/crossfeed/issues/1490/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]